WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:09.749
According to The Economist,
democracy continued its sharp decline in 2020.

00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:12.078
Elected autocrats haven't risen independently

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:15.040
around the world; rather, they learn from one another,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.386
sharing best practices and corrupting
judicial independence and rigging elections.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:23.245
It's now clear that autocrats benefit
from a dictator's playbook.

00:00:23.245 --> 00:00:28.000
It's time for democracies around the world
to author their own democratic playbooks.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.230
Exploiting pre-existing anxieties in society,
electoral re-engineering,

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.120
corrupting the media, jailing political opponents,

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.017
and constitutional reforms to
consolidate these gains—all are key tools

00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:41.520
in the dictator's playbook. Democracies should use

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.559
multilateral forums to put autocrats on notice.

00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:49.280
Sanctions, diplomatic isolation, shoring
up civil society organizations,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.056
and targeted trade measures are but a few of
the tools democracies should use to fight back.

00:00:54.056 --> 00:00:56.320
Further, democracies must reform the UN

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.031
Human Rights Council and bring
the democrats' playbook within the confines

00:01:00.031 --> 00:01:04.000
of a multilateral grouping, like the
proposed D10, to give it greater meaning.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.160
Competing against autocrats
without a playbook is bound to fail.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.640
Should the United
States and other leading democracies

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.159
work to thwart the dictator's playbook
with an offensive plan of their own?

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:18.511
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.520
to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.240
more research and videos from AEI.

